.TH KEY\-TO\-ADDRESSES 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
key\-to\-addresses \- one raw 32\-byte private key per line \-> addresses on every chain in the
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
key\-to\-addresses [\-\-chain LIST] < raw 32\-byte key (hex, WIF, base58, base64, {"key":...}) \-> addresses on every chain
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
table (BTC\-family compressed AND uncompressed, ETH, Tron, XRP, and Solana treating the bytes
as an ed25519 seed). Accepted encodings: 64 hex (0x optional), base64, base58, WIF,
or a JSON line {"key":"..."} / {"wif":"..."}. An ambiguous string is tried in every encoding that yields
exactly 32 bytes; each decoding is a separate "candidate".
Output CONTAINS SECRETS. Thin wrapper around blocktools_secrets::keys. Flags: \-\-chain a,b (default all; zec t1 only when listed).
.SH OPTIONS
See SYNOPSIS; this tool has no separate long\-option list beyond \-\-help.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
or a JSON line {"key":"..."} / {"wif":"..."}. An ambiguous string is tried in every encoding that yields
Output CONTAINS SECRETS. Thin wrapper around blocktools_secrets::keys. Flags: \-\-chain a,b (default all; zec t1 only when listed).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for key\-to\-addresses in recipes/*.md.
| wif, hex_key, b58_key, b64_key | key\-to\-addresses \-\-chain C | input\-raw\-key.md, chain\-*.md |
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
